n bring up Candidate D's strengths and concerns, compare with C. Or we could ask for more info about C's cooperation from other agents. But we can also bring up candidate A's leadership and anticipation of danger, but also concerns about being a show-off and unfriendly. We need to keep discussion systematic.\n\nWe should perhaps challenge the leading candidate C by emphasizing the seriousness of crew cooperation and communication for long-distance flights, and propose that Candidate B might be a stronger overall fit due to stress handling, conscientiousness, and good weather assessment, despite some pretentiousness. Or we could propose Candidate D due to responsibility and problem solving.\n\nWe need to reference explicit facts: For C: \"can make correct decisions quickly\", \"difficulty communicating ideas\", \"regarded as egocentric\", \"not very willing to further his education\". For B: \"very conscientious\", \"handles stress very well\", \"good at assessing weather conditions\", \"excellent computer skills\", \"relatively weak memory for numbers\", \"regarded as pretentious\". For D: \"responds to unexpected events adequately\", \"can concentrate very well\", \"solves problems extremely well\", \"takes responsibility seriously\", \"regarded as a know-it-all\", \"considered moody\". For A: \"can anticipate dangerous situations\", \"able to see complex connections\", \"excellent spatial vision\", \"very good leadership qualities\", \"regarded as a show-off\", \"unfriendly\".\n\nWe need to decide our vote. We could keep Candidate C as provisional but raise concerns, or shift to B or D. Let's think: The panel hasn't discussed A, B, D yet. We need to bring up another candidate. Perhaps we can argue that while C's reliability is strong, the egocentric and communication issues are high risk for crew cooperation, which is essential. Candidate B shows strong stress resilience and conscientiousness, which are critical, and while pretentiousness is a concern, it may be less severe than egocentric communication issues. So we could propose Candidate B as a better overall fit.\n\nThus we can say: I see the points about C, but I think B's stress handling and conscientiousness outweigh C's communication deficits. Provide evidence: B handles stress very well, very conscientious, good weather assessment (technical competence). Concern: pretentious, weak memory for numbers. But memory for numbers may be mitigated by crew cross-checks. So I propose Candidate B as provisional lead.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 2's point. So we say: I appreciate the focus on C, but I have concerns about crew cooperation. I propose B.\n\nThus vote: Candidate B.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
